;; Package pyctypes is pyi's ctypes (queue 244; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, "As built: 244"). This file is libffi's
;; part, played by ci (Arbace's C interpreter): a call interface (ffi_cif) over C types (ffi_type), a call of a C
;; function of the world's program by its address with its arguments' bytes (ffi_call), and closures, Go functions
;; with a C function's address that C code calls (ffi_prep_closure_loc). The world is a C program over one address
;; space (arbace/clib: musl and the libraries a ctypes program loads, linked as one node program), so a pointer
;; ctypes holds is an address C dereferences as is.
;;
;; The argument and result values are bytes as libffi has them (avalue[i] points at an argument of its type's size;
;; an integral result narrower than a word fills a word, widened by its signedness, libffi's ffi_arg), so a port of
;; Modules/_ctypes/callproc.c and callbacks.c calls this as CPython calls libffi. ci's own calling convention is not
;; the psABI's: every argument is a typed value (an integer, a floating value, or an aggregate's bytes copied into
;; the callee's frame) and an aggregate result is written through a hidden first argument, so no register
;; classification (libffi's x86-64 examine_argument) is needed; ffi_prep_cif's layout of an aggregate is the target's
;; (the System V rules: each field at its alignment, the size rounded to the largest), the same as ci's builder's.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[1 1 "// Package pyctypes is pyi's ctypes (queue 244; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 244\"). This file is libffi's"] [2 1 "// part, played by ci (Arbace's C interpreter): a call interface (ffi_cif) over C types (ffi_type), a call of a C"] [3 1 "// function of the world's program by its address with its arguments' bytes (ffi_call), and closures, Go functions"] [4 1 "// with a C function's address that C code calls (ffi_prep_closure_loc). The world is a C program over one address"] [5 1 "// space (arbace/clib: musl and the libraries a ctypes program loads, linked as one node program), so a pointer"] [6 1 "// ctypes holds is an address C dereferences as is."] [7 1 "//"] [8 1 "// The argument and result values are bytes as libffi has them (avalue[i] points at an argument of its type's size;"] [9 1 "// an integral result narrower than a word fills a word, widened by its signedness, libffi's ffi_arg), so a port of"] [10 1 "// Modules/_ctypes/callproc.c and callbacks.c calls this as CPython calls libffi. ci's own calling convention is not"] [11 1 "// the psABI's: every argument is a typed value (an integer, a floating value, or an aggregate's bytes copied into"] [12 1 "// the callee's frame) and an aggregate result is written through a hidden first argument, so no register"] [13 1 "// classification (libffi's x86-64 examine_argument) is needed; ffi_prep_cif's layout of an aggregate is the target's"] [14 1 "// (the System V rules: each field at its alignment, the size rounded to the largest), the same as ci's builder's."] [29 1 "// Kind is a C type's class, libffi's FFI_TYPE_*."] [43 1 "// Ty is a C type as libffi's ffi_type: its size and alignment, and an aggregate's elements (the fields in order,"] [44 1 "// an array's elements repeated; a union is given by ctypes as a struct of its largest member's elements, as"] [45 1 "// Modules/_ctypes/stgdict.c does) with their offsets once laid out."] [54 1 "// The scalar types of ci's target (x86-64, LP64): long double is double (doc/c/SPEC.md §12.5, CS35), 8 bytes,"] [55 1 "// aligned to 8, as on a target whose long double is double."] [72 1 "// ErrBadTypedef and ErrBadArgType are ffi_prep_cif's FFI_BAD_TYPEDEF and FFI_BAD_ARGTYPE."] [78 1 "// Struct is an aggregate of elems, laid out (libffi's initialize_aggregate): each element at the next offset its"] [79 1 "// alignment allows, the size rounded up to the largest alignment."] [118 1 "// CIF is a call interface, ffi_cif: the result's type, the arguments' types, and for a variadic function the"] [119 1 "// number of its fixed arguments (NFixed = len(Args) for a function that is not)."] [126 1 "// PrepCIF is ffi_prep_cif: the interface of a function of the fixed arguments args returning ret."] [129 1 "// PrepCIFVar is ffi_prep_cif_var: a variadic function's interface, its first nfixed arguments fixed; a variable"] [130 1 "// argument must be of a promoted type (no float, no integer narrower than int), else FFI_BAD_ARGTYPE."] [155 1 "// RetSize is the bytes rvalue must hold: a word for an integral result narrower than one (ffi_arg), else the type's."] [166 1 "// toArg is the ci value of an argument of type t whose bytes are b (an aggregate's bytes copied to at, in the"] [167 1 "// world's memory, first)."] [183 1 "// fromArg writes the value a of type t as bytes into b: an integral one widened to a word when word is set (a"] [184 1 "// result, ffi_arg), an aggregate's bytes read at its address."] [229 1 "// World is the C program a ctypes process calls into: one library host (arbace/clib's Lib, its ci program and"] [230 1 "// address space) and its closures."] [236 1 "// NewWorld is the world over the loaded program l."] [239 1 "// push reserves n bytes, aligned to 16, below the C thread's stack pointer, for an aggregate argument or result"] [240 1 "// (as a caller's frame holds them); the caller restores the stack pointer."] [247 1 "// Call is ffi_call: the function at the address fn called with the arguments' bytes avalue (one a parameter, each of"] [248 1 "// its type's size), its result's bytes written into rvalue (cif.RetSize() of them). A C fault or exit inside it ends"] [249 1 "// the process as it would end CPython's (arbace/clib's rule)."] [274 16 "// the mirrors (queue 269): Python code may have changed any object C sees"] [287 1 "// guard runs f, a C fault or exit inside it ending the process as CPython's would end (arbace/clib's Lib.guard),"] [288 1 "// the C thread's stack restored when f panics with anything else (a Python exception a closure raised through C"] [289 1 "// is not one: closures catch theirs, callbacks.c's rule)."] [295 4 "// the world's thread's frames at the fault, innermost first (queue 269: Prog.Trace names the main"] [296 4 "// thread's, which pyctypes does not run on)"] [323 1 "// Closure is a Go function with a C function's address, ffi_closure: C code calling Addr() calls Fn with the"] [324 1 "// arguments' bytes (as avalue) and the result's bytes to fill (cif.RetSize() of them)."] [332 1 "// NewClosure is ffi_prep_closure_loc: a function of the world's program, of the interface cif, whose body is fn."] [347 1 "// Addr is the closure's code address (a C function pointer's value)."] [350 1 "// Free is ffi_closure_free: the address may be given to the next closure; a call through it until then faults."] [362 1 "// call is the closure's native: the call's values made bytes (an aggregate result's address is the hidden first"] [363 1 "// argument), Fn run, its result's bytes made the value C receives."] [380 25 "// the mirrors (queue 269), as a native's"]] :go/pos {:name [15 9] :package [15 1]} :go/semis [[82 22] [104 23] [138 24] [145 23] [294 20] [299 19] [299 40] [336 21]]} (go/file "ffi.go" :doc "Package pyctypes is pyi's ctypes (queue 244; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 244\"). This file is libffi's\npart, played by ci (Arbace's C interpreter): a call interface (ffi_cif) over C types (ffi_type), a call of